# VitalSense — Cursor Rules
# Canonical source: .github/instructions/copilot-instructions.md and CLAUDE.md
# This file keeps Cursor IDE aligned with VS Code Copilot instructions.

## Quick Reference

- **Branding**: Always "VitalSense" in user-facing text — never "Health App"
- **Stack**: React 19 + TypeScript + Vite, Tailwind v4, Radix UI, TanStack Query, Cloudflare Workers (Hono), iOS (Swift/HealthKit)
- **Path alias**: @/* → ./src/*

## Critical Rules

1. TypeScript + ESM only. No require, no CommonJS, no `any`.
2. Zod validation at all data boundaries. Fail closed on parse errors.
3. No PII or raw health data in logs.
4. Workers-safe APIs only (Request, Response, fetch, crypto). No Node.js APIs in Worker code.
5. Secrets via c.env bindings. Never hardcode.
6. Tailwind v4 utilities + semantic tokens from src/main.css. No CSS-in-JS.
7. React Query for server state. Co-locate query keys.
8. Radix UI + existing src/components/ui/* — don't recreate primitives.
9. Colocated tests: *.test.ts(x) next to source, Vitest + @testing-library/react.
10. SwiftLint: WARNING >120 chars, ERROR >150 chars. No force_unwrapping.

## Commands

- pnpm validate — Full CI (lint + type-check + test)
- pnpm dev — Start dev server
- pnpm cf:dev — Local Workers preview
- pnpm cf:deploy — Deploy to dev
- pnpm deploy:prod — Deploy to production

